        <div id="contribution-model" class="content-card">
          
          
          <h2><span class="i18n-en">Model</span></h2>
          <div class="content-body">
            

            
              
            <p><span class="i18n-en">Computational from end to end, which makes it the part another team can run without a lab. Three outputs: a docking pipeline that narrows a candidate panel, an atomic-level account of how the gating peptides sit on their receptors, and the files that reproduce both.</span></p>

              
            
              
            
            <h3 id="model-screening" data-no-fold><span class="i18n-en">Seventeen candidates, one lead</span></h3>

              
            
              
            <p><span class="i18n-en">Screening a nanobody panel costs reagent and weeks. We replaced the first pass with two docking stages, a rigid ClusPro sweep over the whole panel and HADDOCK 2.5 semi-flexible refinement on what survived, and added a specificity index so that H1N1-selective binders separate from cross-reactive ones instead of everything ranking by docking score. Seventeen candidates became one lead, R1aB6, with no binding assay run.</span></p>

              
            
              
            <p><span class="i18n-en">A team with a panel and no structures can repeat this on predicted models and order a shortlist instead of a library. The specificity index is the part worth taking, because without it the ranking collapses back into "best score wins", which is how cross-reactive binders get ordered. No binding assay has confirmed the ranking.</span></p>

              
            
              
            
            <h3 id="model-gating" data-no-fold><span class="i18n-en">Both gating interfaces</span></h3>

              
            
              
            <p><span class="i18n-en">An inhibitory-peptide gate only works if blocking the outside leaves the inside intact. We tested that on both systems: hM1Dq with the MT1 peptide and Ste2 with MT1_5, each membrane-aligned before docking, refined in HADDOCK, then run through CHARMM-GUI membrane building, 100 ns GROMACS dynamics, SPICE interface analysis and gmx_MMPBSA. Both come out the same way, with the peptide in the orthosteric site and the intracellular G-protein interface left free.</span></p>

              
            
              
            <p><span class="i18n-en">That is a check on an assumption, not a demonstration of gating in cells, and it is written as the former. The workflow is the reusable part: it transfers to any receptor and peptide pair, including ones with no experimental structure.</span></p>

              
            
              
            
            <h3 id="model-hotspot" data-no-fold><span class="i18n-en">One hotspot, one hypothesis</span></h3>

              
            
              
            <p><span class="i18n-en">One number did most of the work here. Per-residue decomposition of the R1aB6–HA complex puts ARG-B:31 at −5.46 kcal/mol, well clear of its neighbours, which turns into a single experiment: make R31A and measure it by SPR or ELISA.</span></p>

              
            
              
            <p><span class="i18n-en">That is what a model is good for, choosing the next experiment rather than illustrating the last one. A team with a docked complex and no assay capacity can run the same decomposition and come out with one residue to mutate, which is far cheaper than scanning an interface. The mutation is designed and the measurement is planned; neither has been run.</span></p>

              
            
              
            
            <h3 id="model-reproducibility" data-no-fold><span class="i18n-en">The pipeline as files</span></h3>

              
            
              
            <p><span class="i18n-en">A pipeline published without its inputs is a figure, not a tool. HADDOCK and ClusPro inputs, parameter files and analysis scripts are kept with the work, and the 9VH4 complex is re-docked through the same pipeline as a positive control so the numbers have something to sit against.</span></p>

              
            
              
            <p><span class="i18n-en">The docking results also became an interactive card game, which is the form we use when the audience is not a modelling audience. Both are on the Model page; the game runs there rather than as a download.</span></p>

              
            
              
            <ul class="link-list link-list--section-end">
              
